  "question": {
    "professionCode": "frontend_developer",
    "level": "senior",
    "difficulty": "advanced",
    "questionText": "Как диагностировать сетевые проблемы между Docker контейнерами?",
    "shortAnswer": "Top-down: same network (inspect) → DNS (getent, 127.0.0.11) → ping IP → nc port → ss bind → iptables DOCKER-USER → tcpdump. Default bridge без DNS. 127.0.0.1 bind — classic error.",
    "idealAnswer": "Checklist: 1) inspect Networks same? network connect if not. 2) DNS getent hosts db — only user-defined bridge, 127.0.0.11 resolver. Default bridge no DNS. 3) ping IP. 4) nc -vz port — refused vs timeout. 5) ss -tlnp — 127.0.0.1:5432 unreachable from peers, fix 0.0.0.0. 6) iptables DOCKER-USER, UFW. 7) tcpdump br-*. Overlay: MTU 1450, UDP 4789. host network Linux only; Mac → host.docker.internal. netshoot --network=container:app. Ошибки: default bridge; 127.0.0.1 bind; iptables outside DOCKER-USER; --link.",
    "maxScore": 10,
    "skills": [
      "docker"
    ]
  },
